
######## Friday, the 2nd of January, 1931 — the day after New Year's Day (cold and wet (-2° to 6°C)) ########
   ◆ Ada's past: He has never been known to refuse a request for assistance from a fellow-worker in distress.
   ◆ Arthur's past: He never spends more than half his income.
   ◆ Mr. Thomas's past: He has remembered, all his life, that, when he was a little boy, his father died, and left him five pounds.
   📅 Ada means to: Monday: washes the floor, and gets Bert's dinner ready | Tuesday: cleans the windows, and buys coal | Wednesday: washes the clothes, and gets Bert's supper ready | Thursday: mends the stockings, and clear off the week's dust | Friday: pays the rent, and goes to chapel
   📅 Arthur means to: Monday: sees about getting shoes for Joan
   📅 Mr. Thomas means to: Monday: sees to the insurance of his household goods | Tuesday: pays the milk bill | Wednesday: goes to Sydenham, to collect a debt of ten pounds from Mr | Thursday: pays the butcher
