   ◇ Ada reflects: She thinks her a respectable, hard-working person, in needy circumstances.
   ◇ Ada reflects: She thinks him a cad, because he has treated her badly.
   ◇ Arthur reflects: He thinks him a humbug, because he pretends to be sorry for the Turner family, and yet does nothing to help them.
   ◇ Arthur reflects: He thinks her extravagant, because the housekeeping money has run out.
   ◇ Arthur reflects: He thinks her a deserving person, because she has lost her place through no fault of her own.
