   📅 Mr. Thomas means to: Monday: balances his cash, settle with Mrs | Tuesday: completes the audit, and on Wednesday go to the seaside

--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Sunday, the 11th of January, 1931 (1/5 key facts kept) ---
To-day I spoke civilly to a stranger in a public-house, and he lent me two shillings.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Sunday, the 11th of January, 1931 (6/6 key facts kept) ---
Finished audit books.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Sunday, the 11th of January, 1931 (1/1 key facts kept) ---
To-day I read in The Times the death of the Princess Royal. The office was not cleaned this morning, and Mrs. Turner did not come (twice). I gave Mrs. Turner notice for not coming to clean, and told Mr. Hale that the auditors come on Monday.
   ☾ Ada: She dreamt that she was cleaning an office in King William Street, City, and the gentleman who engaged her said, "Very well done, Mrs. Turner, very well done indeed; I am pleased."
      📖 It foretells employment.
   ☾ Arthur (forgotten by morning): He dreamt that he was being examined by the auditors, and that everything was all right.

